  "dataset": "One server per model with --draft-policy fixed --draft-tokens 15 --draft-trace, thinking off, context 40960, sessions 1. 46 requests per model: sampled at temperature 1, top-k 64, top-p 0.95, repeat penalty 1.0 (12 prose prompts x 256 tokens, 12 story seeds x 128, 6 code-write seeds x 384, 3 code-edit seeds x 384, 3 essay seeds x 400 over the ~31K-token document), and greedy (6 prose, code-write, code-edit, repetitive, essay). Workloads from tools/gemma4/draft_policy_bench.py. Complete chains (15 verified proposals, no copies): ~2,300 sampled and ~680 greedy per model. Requests alternate between development and held-out sets within each workload.",
  "labels": "Each row: acceptance probability given the rows before it accepted (greedy 0/1, sampled min(1, p/q)); each runner-up: sibling hit probability (VerifyWithSibling second stage). Expected tokens of any stopping decision are exact given the labels; costs are the policy price tables.",
  "replay": "gemma4_draft_replay simulate (production DraftCalibration/CalibratedChain via a replica checked against production on every chain), 16 replicas of online learning with outcomes drawn from the labels.",
  "feature_study": "Python (numpy 2.5.2, scikit-learn 1.9.0): reach-weighted soft-label logistic models fitted on development rows, scored on held-out rows; each model then drives a copy of the stopping rule (no siblings) on held-out chains.",
